****

A continuum image of the Sun, for reference. It shows the Sun as it appears visually, sunspots with umbra and penumbra, active regions, granulae.
It was obtained through direct imaging. A band pass filter was used to limit chromatic issues, dispersion and aberation,
and a bluer wavelength was chosen, to maximize the angular resolution/aperture ratio (Rayleigh criterion) given the decent seeing conditions. 

Coincidentally, the filter is centered onto hydrogen beta, and indeed, prominences may show up, when overexposing, 
but FWHM 3nm is wide enough for the spectral line to be overwhelmed by the continuum of the photosphere.